<!--
	Managed-code-stripping preservation for Visual State Machine V3 (IL2CPP / high stripping).

	VSM drives itself by reflection on data stored in graph assets:
	  - states are instantiated from their assembly-qualified name
	    (StateMachineInstance -> Activator.CreateInstance),
	  - [Transition] / [DataIn] / [DataOut] fields are bound by name,
	  - blackboard values are (de)serialized through reflected generic handlers.
	None of those references are visible to the managed linker, so under
	Managed Stripping Level = Medium/High the built-in states and reflected
	members can be removed, causing runtime failures. This file keeps VSM's own
	runtime assemblies intact.

	Scope: this preserves VSM's assemblies only. User-defined state types and
	custom blackboard value types live in other assemblies and must be preserved
	by the consuming project (its own link.xml, [Preserve], or
	[assembly: AlwaysLinkAssembly]). See the documentation for details.

	preserve="all" is deliberately conservative (correctness over size); it can be
	narrowed later if WebGL build size becomes a concern.
-->
<linker>
	<assembly fullname="Nonatomic.VSM.Runtime" preserve="all" />
	<assembly fullname="Nonatomic.VSM.Visualization" preserve="all" />
</linker>
